# mcp-server-competitor-content

Cursor agent rules. Follow on every change.

## Scope
- Work only inside this repository.
- Layer order: infrastructure → engines → services → tools → server.

## Architecture
- All HTML fetch/parse via ContentFetcher. No fetch/cheerio in engines/services.
- NLP engines are pure: content in → structured result out. No HTTP.
- Never scrape Google SERPs directly — use serpProvider only.
- Headless (Playwright) only after thin static content; never default path.
- Cache robots.txt rulesets by domain (ROBOTS_CACHE_TTL_SECONDS).
- Default clustering: TF-IDF + cosine. Embeddings only if EMBEDDING_PROVIDER set.
- Services never import @modelcontextprotocol/sdk.

## TypeScript
- Strict: noImplicitAny, strictNullChecks, exactOptionalPropertyTypes.
- Explicit return types; never any; prefer readonly.
- Functions under 40 lines; one tool per file.

## Errors
- McpError with codes: InvalidParams, SCRAPE_FAIL, PARSE_ERROR, ROBOTS_DISALLOWED,
  RATE_LIMITED, NO_CONTENT, SERP_PROVIDER_UNCONFIGURED, HEADLESS_RENDER_FAIL, SSRF_BLOCKED.
- Zod validate inputs. No stack leaks to clients.

## Testing
- Mock all HTTP, SERP, and headless. Use fixtures including thin SPA HTML.
- ≥80% branch coverage engines + services.
